{"agent":"Monster3-NV-next-tag-filter-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The lane branch computes `tags = _tags(a)` but then calls `_api().next_lane(...)` without passing `tags`, so `--tag`/`--wave` are silently ignored whenever `--lane` is used. For example, `ddflow next --lane <lane> --tag wave:3` (or `--wave 3`) can return ready/blocked items from that lane that lack `wave:3`, and an unknown tag in lane mode is not refused, contrary to the declared `next` parameters and the added workflow help.","digest":"70d472f1d4c394f7","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/navigate.py:_next","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/navigate.py:_next"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`test_tag_limits_ready_and_blocked` does not actually exercise blocked filtering. The `_queue` fixture creates tasks with no dependencies or other blocking conditions, so `d[\"blocked\"]` is empty for the `--tag x` call; the assertion `all(b[\"item\"] in {\"M.A\", \"M.B\"} for b in d[\"blocked\"])` is therefore vacuously true. If the implementation failed to filter blocked items—for example, if an untagged task that is blocked by a dependency were returned in `blocked`—this test would still pass, despite the intent requiring that both ready and blocked be limited to the tag.","digest":"dc7864e4fb24dffd","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_next_tag_filter.py:74-78","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_next_tag_filter.py:74-78"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The new `_queue` fixture violates the recorded project rule [r-task-phase-needs-wave]: every task must name a phase, state dependencies in `needs`, and carry a `wave:N` tag, with `no-deps` for prerequisite-free work. Here `M.A`, `M.B`, and `N.C` have wave tags but no `no-deps` despite having no `--needs`, and `N.D` is created with no tags at all, so it has neither a wave tag nor `no-deps`.","digest":"779e8852d30b166a","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_next_tag_filter.py:13-64","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_next_tag_filter.py:13-64"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`candidates = with_tags(candidates, tags)` filters the candidate items *before* the planning and cap computation loop (`plan()` body), violating the requirement: \"Filter applied to the candidates BEFORE the cap cut, so the cap is computed over the whole queue as now.\" Because `candidates` is restricted to only those matching `tags` prior to calculating parallelism limits, slot counts, and ready/blocked partitions, the cap is computed exclusively over the filtered slice rather than the whole queue.","digest":"ec5b8b932ce07816","family":"google","location":"ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py:289","malformed":"","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py:289"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`--tag` / `--wave` are declared on the same `next` command as `--lane`, and `_tags` is computed for every call, but the `--lane` branch still calls `next_lane` without `tags`. Given a lane that offers both `M.A` (tag `x`) and `N.D` (no `x`), `ddflow next --lane that-lane --tag x` returns `N.D` in ready or blocked. That is the stated falsifier: an item lacking the tag appears, and the flag is silently ignored rather than exiting 1 or intersecting.","digest":"6f484236ca64a41f","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/navigate.py:_next","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/navigate.py:_next"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14117,"diff_sha":"7e6f9ae1db7020a2a9a0574d25ce9c645c5aea229222dd7d8bf8fb3b232cf6c7","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/NV-next-tag-filter","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.3,"family":"alibaba","findings":5,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"822ee0d3a02a8a7d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/NV-next-tag-filter.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261112T144718Z-a0620f9c.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-NV-next-tag-filter-7267fe reviewed lane-next-view's NV-next-tag-filter","reviewed_head":"4ee9fd72b73524fe6c0b2956ebbe9b5b6a53dcfa","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lifecycle/planning.py":"100644 16ca86f1a1bd7ee3db0983b18fc9a3dd6d888e08","ddflow/api/lifecycle/ready.py":"100644 21b1a92a2ca8f7db80ff08e91f0700d6945e4a76","ddflow/core/schedule/__init__.py":"100644 463b9aac30751eec7ce5209bc1211f4428b35959","ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py":"100644 fd63115f8244a1c83f39e419181a128095325448","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/navigate.py":"100644 7623326ee0db61a41ac5b0c5f4fcb4bd1872b4fd","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/workflow.md":"100644 eb7d72e94671e97e169c2d25c250c5b6d4c0a5ed","tests/test_next_tag_filter.py":"100644 4805dc188627e8d6a721a43c8a2844dbe4d1ee7a"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/navigate.py:_next","tests/test_next_tag_filter.py:74-78","tests/test_next_tag_filter.py:13-64","ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py:289","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle/navigate.py:_next"],"tree_sha":"4ee9fd72b735+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"5 finding(s)"},"id":"e560432a53accdfdad2b2cdde","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":184259,"schema":1,"subject":"NV-next-tag-filter","ts":"2026-11-12T14:48:54.228048Z"}
